  "conclusions": [
    "The existing linux-armhf libraries match the official kindlehf ARM EABI hard-float calling convention. They do not match the official kindlepw2 soft-float calling convention.",
    "The WASM host requires clock_gettime@GLIBC_2.17 and __isoc99_sscanf@GLIBC_2.7; the remaining versioned imports are GLIBC_2.4.",
    "The portable crypto library imports only GLIBC_2.4 symbols, although it was built with the same generic .2.17 target baseline.",
    "Both plugin libraries need libpthread.so.0 in addition to their other recorded dependencies, even though neither has a pthread_* undefined import.",
    "The official KOReader LuaJIT version needs do not establish the firmware libc version, and the official ZIPs do not contain a complete system runtime.",
    "The official toolchain loader has DT_VERSYM and is not an empty linker stub. The parent-observed bootstrap assertion occurs before Lua and plugin loading; its root cause is not established by this static review.",
    "A successful independent ARM/sysroot fixture run would be compatibility evidence for that userspace, not physical Scribe hardware or a captured firmware-image verification."
  ]
}
